From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] lynx: build against android-mainline

  * Kconfig.ext.lynx: drop the radio/samsung/s5300 and touch/common sources.
    gs201's Kconfig.ext already sources both and device_build() concatenates
    the two; android-mainline's kconfig rejects the repeat ("repeated
    inclusion of ..."), so the lynx kernel_config failed.

lynx-linus-mainline (android-mainline -> Linus' v7.3):
  * dts/gs201-lynx-usecases.dtsi: max77759,extbst-ctl gets its "-gpios"
    suffix. The charger asks gpiolib for con_id "max77759,extbst-ctl"; the
    Android Common Kernels resolve that through a gpiolib-of rename quirk
    for this exact property, which Linus' gpiolib does not have.
  * Kbuild for the ddk_modules here, generated from BUILD.bazel by
    tools/bazel2kbuild.py, for the make-only build (kernel/kbuild.mk):
      display/Kbuild
---
diff --git a/Kconfig.ext.lynx b/Kconfig.ext.lynx
index 6060313..66ef8d9 100644
--- a/Kconfig.ext.lynx
+++ b/Kconfig.ext.lynx
@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 
-source "$(KCONFIG_EXT_MODULES_PREFIX)private/google-modules/radio/samsung/s5300/Kconfig"
-
-source "$(KCONFIG_EXT_MODULES_PREFIX)private/google-modules/touch/common/Kconfig"
+# junkyard (lynx-mainline): radio/samsung/s5300 and touch/common used to be
+# sourced here too, but gs201's Kconfig.ext.gs201 already sources both and
+# device_build() concatenates the two files. 6.18's kconfig tolerated the
+# repeat; android-mainline's rejects it ("repeated inclusion of ..."), and the
+# lynx kernel_config fails. Nothing lynx-specific remains to source.
diff --git a/display/Kbuild b/display/Kbuild
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..25d765d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/display/Kbuild
@@ -0,0 +1,105 @@
